OL,3,GNEWSAAssembly debating bill aimed at
OL,4,Abanning conversion practices
OL,5,
OL,6,FA bill aimed at banning sexuality and
OL,7,Fgender conversion practices is being
OL,8,Fdebated by assembly members for the
OL,9,Ffirst time at Stormont.
OL,11,FIt contains provisions that could see a
OL,12,Ftwo-year jail sentence imposed on
OL,13,Fpeople who conduct conversion
OL,14,Fpractices.
OL,16,FAlliance's deputy leader Eoin Tennyson
OL,17,Fproposed the private member's
OL,18,Flegislation, but it has been criticised
OL,19,Fby the Democratic Unionist Party (DUP)
OL,20,Fwhich said the bill "presents a real
OL,21,Fthreat to freedom".
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
